  "question": {
    "text": "The presence of soluble fluoride ion upto 1 ppm concentration in drinking water, is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "harmful for teeth",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "harmful to skin",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "harmful to bones",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "safe for teeth",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Soluble fluoride is often added to drinking water to make concentration upto 1 ppm because F&ndash; ions make the enamel on teeth much harder. But above 2 ppm cause brown mottling of teeth. Cause harmful effect on bones and teeth."
  }
